                <note rend="inline" type="source">890g.01/216: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-22T13:00:00+01:00">June 22, 1929—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 22—9:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>165. Your 151, June 21, 4 p.m. Foreign Office states that inquiry was sent to
                    Baghdad in this matter some weeks ago but that no reply has been received. No
                    difficulties are anticipated and efforts will be made to expedite action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
